  - Supplying a valid Azure access token or API key to litellm before calling acompletion.
  - Retrying the same acompletion call and confirming it returns a successful response (HTTP 200/OK at the wrapper level).

Pitfalls and environment quirks
- Calling litellm.acompletion without configuring provider-specific credentials will fail with AuthenticationError.
- Misconfigured or missing Azure credentials (e.g., access token not set, expired, or malformed) will trigger “Unauthorized. Access token is missing or invalid.”
- Ensure model/provider routing matches the credentials you have configured (e.g., do not route to Azure when only Anthropic credentials are present).

